{"id":"0fc807c50c29cdf1","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-thm-measurable-iterated.md","title":"Countable Iteration of a Normal Measure","display":"thm-measurable-iterated — Countable Iteration of a Normal Measure","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-measurable-iterated","aliases":["58-thm-measurable-iterated"],"display":"thm-measurable-iterated — Countable Iteration of a Normal Measure","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-thm-iterated-ultrapowers.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-measurable-iterated"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-measurable-iterated</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-measurable-iterated — Countable Iteration of a Normal Measure"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"0d480b0822a231c2\" href=\"?note=0d480b0822a231c2\" title=\"../batch02/58-thm-iterated-ultrapowers.md\">../batch02/58-thm-iterated-ultrapowers.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U,\\kappa\\in V\">\\(U,\\kappa\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormalMeasure}_S(U,\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{NormalMeasure}_S(U,\\kappa)\\)</span> is the predicate used by <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0d480b0822a231c2\" href=\"?note=0d480b0822a231c2\" title=\"../batch02/58-thm-iterated-ultrapowers.md\">../batch02/58-thm-iterated-ultrapowers.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}\">\\(\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\)</span> is the metatheoretic class quantifier; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal M_n\">\\(\\mathcal M_n\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"j_{n,m}\">\\(j_{n,m}\\)</span> are class objects.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ClassElementaryEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{ClassElementaryEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ult}^{\\mathrm{Cls}}\">\\(\\operatorname{Ult}^{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WF}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{WF}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span> are the explicitly expanded metanotions of the cited theorem.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}measurable\\text{-}iterated}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{NormalMeasure}_S(U,\\kappa)\n\\to\n\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\mathcal M,\\mathcal J\\;\n\\exists\\vec U,\\vec\\kappa\\in V^{\\omega+1}\\;\n\\left[\n\\mathcal M_0=\\mathbf V\\land U_0=U\\land\\kappa_0=\\kappa\n\\right.\\\\\n\\left.\n\\land\\forall n&lt;\\omega\\;\\left(\n\\mathcal M_{n+1}\\cong\n\\operatorname{Ult}^{\\mathrm{Cls}}(\\mathcal M_n,U_n,\\kappa_n)\n\\land\n\\mathrm{ClassElementaryEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\n(j_{n,n+1};\\mathcal M_n,\\mathcal M_{n+1})\n\\land U_{n+1}=j_{n,n+1}(U_n)\n\\land\\kappa_{n+1}=j_{n,n+1}(\\kappa_n)\n\\right)\\\\\n\\land\\forall n\\leq m\\leq\\omega\\;\n\\mathrm{ClassElementaryEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\n(j_{n,m};\\mathcal M_n,\\mathcal M_m)\n\\land\\forall n\\leq m\\leq\\ell\\leq\\omega\\;\n(j_{n,\\ell}=j_{m,\\ell}\\circ j_{n,m})\n\\land\\forall n\\leq\\omega\\;\\mathrm{WF}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\mathcal M_n)\n\\land\\mathcal M_\\omega\\cong\n\\varinjlim_{n&lt;\\omega}(\\mathcal M_n,j_{n,m})\n\\right].\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}measurable\\text{-}iterated}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{NormalMeasure}_S(U,\\kappa)\n\\to\n\\exists^{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\mathcal M,\\mathcal J\\;\n\\exists\\vec U,\\vec\\kappa\\in V^{\\omega+1}\\;\n\\left[\n\\mathcal M_0=\\mathbf V\\land U_0=U\\land\\kappa_0=\\kappa\n\\right.\\\\\n\\left.\n\\land\\forall n&lt;\\omega\\;\\left(\n\\mathcal M_{n+1}\\cong\n\\operatorname{Ult}^{\\mathrm{Cls}}(\\mathcal M_n,U_n,\\kappa_n)\n\\land\n\\mathrm{ClassElementaryEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\n(j_{n,n+1};\\mathcal M_n,\\mathcal M_{n+1})\n\\land U_{n+1}=j_{n,n+1}(U_n)\n\\land\\kappa_{n+1}=j_{n,n+1}(\\kappa_n)\n\\right)\\\\\n\\land\\forall n\\leq m\\leq\\omega\\;\n\\mathrm{ClassElementaryEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{meta}}\n(j_{n,m};\\mathcal M_n,\\mathcal M_m)\n\\land\\forall n\\leq m\\leq\\ell\\leq\\omega\\;\n(j_{n,\\ell}=j_{m,\\ell}\\circ j_{n,m})\n\\land\\forall n\\leq\\omega\\;\\mathrm{WF}^{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\mathcal M_n)\n\\land\\mathcal M_\\omega\\cong\n\\varinjlim_{n&lt;\\omega}(\\mathcal M_n,j_{n,m})\n\\right].\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega+1\">\\(\\omega+1\\)</span> projection actually supported by the cited iterated-ultrapower theorem.  The former arbitrary-ordinal claim required a separate transfinite recursion and limit-stage construction that was not among its dependencies.</li>\n<li>Since the iterates of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> are proper classes, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal M\">\\(\\mathcal M\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal J\">\\(\\mathcal J\\)</span> are bound by class quantifiers rather than ordinary set quantifiers.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-thm-iterated-ultrapowers.md","status":"resolved","id":"0d480b0822a231c2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-thm-iterated-ultrapowers.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-thm-iterated-ultrapowers.md","status":"re